{"repositoryId":1156525120,"availability":"available","full":"ProjectASAP/ASAPQuery","name":"ASAPQuery","description":"Drop-in Acceleration of SQL/PromQL queries","category":"Other","language":"Rust","stars":52,"forks":2,"created":"2026-02-12T18:43:32Z","updated":"2026-10-15T14:52:33Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://projectasap.github.io/","topics":[],"demo":"https://projectasap.github.io/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:04.908Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:04.908Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:04.908Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T15:01:04.908Z","stars":52,"forks":2}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["ASAPQuery is a drop-in query accelerator for queries in various languages like PromQL and SQL. ASAPQuery delivers:","The current version of ASAPQuery works with a Prometheus-Grafana stack. We are extending it to work seamlessly with a Clickhouse-Grafana stack.","ASAPQuery sits between Prometheus and Grafana. It intercepts queries from Grafana and answers them using streaming sketches, instead of scanning large volumes of raw data in Prometheus. It ingests data using Prometheus' remotewrite interface. ASAPQuery also targets other observability systems (e.g. VictoriaMetrics) and time-series databases (e.g. Clickhouse, Elastic)."],"features":["100x latency reduction for various complex aggregate queries such as quantiles","Lower CPU and memory usage during querying","Ease-of-use with your existing tech stack"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ProjectASAP/ASAPQuery/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"4e706dbacb86eecf290d9b93e41bc25e9ca86ca58f114803916f378dd080c0a8","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:05.334Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:05.334Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"ASAPQuery is a drop-in query accelerator for queries in various languages like PromQL and SQL. ASAPQuery delivers:","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ProjectAS